{
 "schema": "snapwright.catalog/0.2",
 "note": "Part IDs follow BrickLink/LDraw numbering. 'core' colours are widely produced in the basic brick/plate/tile moulds listed here; 'limited' colours exist but not in every mould. `availability` lists, per part, the colours it has appeared in (plain, unprinted) in sets since `availability_meta.since`, from Rebrickable's CSV downloads; refresh it with `sw.py sync-catalog`. The packer only uses listed combos (the 1x1 brick, plate and tile excepted, as a fallback the checks flag). `rebrickable` is set where Rebrickable numbers a part differently. Schema 0.2 adds connection metadata: `top` / `bottom` list the part's cells (i along L from the back/high row, j along W) that have a stud on top / take a stud underneath ('all' or 'none' for simple parts); `shape` is box, slope, slope_inv or round; `ldraw` is the LDraw file and `ldraw_origin` where its origin sits (top: top centre; stud_row_top: top centre of the back row; bottom: bottom centre). `auto` parts may be placed by the surface-shaping pass. `side` lists cells (i, j) with a stud on the part's side face; side studs point along the part's local +z (LDraw -Z) and sit `side_mm` above the part's bottom.",
